# What never enters git. Two groups: ordinary build output and dependencies, and the CV
# tree, which carries a phone number and URLs derived from a secret.

node_modules
dist
.env
.DS_Store
*.bak
.claude
.devswarm/
plans/
status.md

# Every CV is generated during the build, and a committed PDF is permanent because git
# history keeps it after any deletion. Matched anywhere in the tree, because a stray copy is
# how the private CV escapes. `git add -f` overrides deliberately.
*.pdf

# The whole private CV tree. Ignored by its fixed public parent rather than by the segment
# under it, because each segment is derived from the secret and is a working URL, so naming
# one here would put it in a committed file.
public/cv/

# The same tree wherever a stray copy of public/ lands it. The directory name is itself
# the secret, so committing the index.html inside it publishes that CV.

# Exact rather than `**/cv/*/`, so a real source directory added under cv/ later is not
# silently ignored. It matches only the shape cv/build-pdf.mjs produces.
**/cv/*-[0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f]/

# A build artefact, regenerated every run. Unlike the tree above it names only /cv/*, which
# is public, so this is housekeeping rather than secrecy.
public/_headers

# The private field values and that directory name.
cv/private.local.json

# Scratch copies of the CV. They carry the private fields inline and are not part of the
# build, so a stray `git add .` should not be able to commit one.
cv/* copy*.html
cv/*.local.html
